#!/usr/bin/env bash

BOYS the plan is simple

If this world wants a specialty, my specialty is learning, I can do anything and everything, I will learn everything.

Objective: Master Ultralearning
Description: figure out what is slowing my learning, and what optimizes my learning
Good:
- Keep it simple, 3 big projects a day, varying between days is the ideal thing
- Intercaling them with a 24 minutes period to let it on, and 2 hours to get in power mode
- If you get stucked we have commodities: 2 showers, 1 sleep, Water Walks, Exercising, Help Someone, Eating Yummy, Coffee, Alone Game
- Work more modular and desechable, so that you can throw away what it doesnt work and have what it works with you
- For resting breaks we have an hour and 24 min of: Ultralearning, Japanese, Design, Dvorak
- Obsidian takes too long, UI also takes too long in general, removing unnecessary stuff, automating necessary

Bad:
- Doing while thinking is easy and you can do it, then you have to up the difficulty
- Giving you too much liberties, you much restrict it to make you more creative
- Not strict enough with the tasks
- Have not set a clear start and a clear end
- Scared to fail and lose progress, since it may not be the most optimal
- You always do simulations, and not the real thing, which is totally different
- No way of tracking performance, like distractions or interruptions, wasted time, amount learned
- You dont do the most important things at the start of the day, so the hardest one to start

